diff --git a/sway/sway-input.5.scd b/sway/sway-input.5.scd
index 18744a2..c903297 100644
--- a/sway/sway-input.5.scd
+++ b/sway/sway-input.5.scd
@@ -94,6 +94,51 @@ The following commands may only be used in the configuration file.
 *input* <identifier> xkb_numlock enabled|disabled
 	Initially enables or disables NumLock on startup, the default is disabled.
 
+## KEYBOARD ACCESSIBILITY CONFIGURATION
+
+These options change how key presses are interpreted, for users who have
+difficulty pressing several keys at once, holding keys briefly, or using a
+pointing device. Each keyboard keeps its own state: keyboards with any of these
+options enabled are never grouped (see *keyboard_grouping* below).
+
+*input* <identifier> sticky_keys enabled|disabled
+	Enables or disables sticky keys, the default is disabled. Tapping Shift,
+	Control, Alt or Super latches it: it applies to the next key that is not
+	one of these modifiers. Tapping a latched modifier again locks it until it
+	is tapped once more. Holding a modifier while pressing another key works as
+	usual.
+
+*input* <identifier> sticky_keys_two_key_off enabled|disabled
+	With sticky keys enabled, pressing two modifiers at the same time releases
+	all latched and locked modifiers. The default is enabled.
+
+*input* <identifier> slow_keys <milliseconds>
+	A key press only counts once the key has been held for the given number of
+	milliseconds; shorter presses are ignored. The default is 0, which disables
+	slow keys.
+
+*input* <identifier> bounce_keys <milliseconds>
+	Ignores a press of a key that comes within the given number of milliseconds
+	after the previous accepted press of the same key. The default is 0, which
+	disables bounce keys.
+
+*input* <identifier> mouse_keys enabled|disabled
+	Enables or disables mouse keys, the default is disabled. The keypad keys 1
+	to 4 and 6 to 9 move the pointer in their direction instead of being sent to
+	applications, whatever the state of NumLock.
+
+*input* <identifier> mouse_keys_init_delay <milliseconds>
+	Sets the time between pressing a mouse key and the start of the pointer
+	motion. The default is 300 milliseconds.
+
+*input* <identifier> mouse_keys_accel_time <milliseconds>
+	Sets the time the pointer takes to reach its maximum speed once it starts
+	moving. The default is 300 milliseconds.
+
+*input* <identifier> mouse_keys_max_speed <pixels per second>
+	Sets the maximum speed of the pointer, in pixels per second. The default is
+	1000.
+
 ## TABLET CONFIGURATION
 
 *input* <identifier> tool_mode <tool> <absolute|relative>
